silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_03_embedded_engine_functors_sections_02_functor_preservation_laws_concrete_anchor_source_obj silm:hasLongDescription "The VetRecord_Mittens_SourceObject is X is the source federation object — concretely VetRecord_Mittens in the Mittens example. It is the domain of the functor input morphism. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'X (source federation object)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
