silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_03_embedded_engine_functors_sections_02_functor_preservation_laws_concrete_anchor_functor_node silm:hasLongDescription "The FunctorPreservationLawsFunctorNode is F is the FunctorPreservationLaws functor — it maps typed federation objects and morphisms from the source category to the target category, preserving composition and identity. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F (the FunctorPreservationLaws functor)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
